abstract: >-
  The Torso Processing ToolBox (TPTBox) is a Python package for processing
  BIDS-compliant medical imaging datasets (CT, MRI), with a focus on torso and
  spine analysis. It provides NIfTI I/O, reorientation and resampling, Points of
  Interest computation for vertebrae, 2D and 3D snapshots, registration,
  stitching, and segmentation integrations.
keywords:
  - medical imaging
  - BIDS
  - NIfTI
  - spine
  - segmentation
  - registration
  - computed tomography
  - magnetic resonance imaging
